id: pm-inn5y5
title: "Acceptance criteria are documented as merging like tags but are stored as one delimiter-joined scalar, so concurrent criteria additions from different branches are silently discarded"
description: "src/core/item/parse.ts:92 documents applyAcceptanceCriteriaMutations as giving --add-ac/--remove-ac 'tag-API parity' with the explicit promise that 'disjoint additions merge cleanly across branches'. Tags have that property because 'tags' is in ITEM_UNION_COLLECTION_FIELDS and merges by element identity. acceptance_criteria is not in that list: it is stored as a single string joined with '; ', so it takes the scalar three-way path and resolves toward the preferred side like any other scalar. The documented guarantee is therefore false for the one field whose CLI grammar is explicitly list-shaped. Criteria are the field close-validation reads, so the loss is silent in exactly the workflow that is supposed to be enforced."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: acceptance-criteria,concurrency,data-loss,merge
created_at: "2026-08-02T21:05:22.040Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-03T17:40:42.440Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-03T17:40:41.940Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-03T17:40:41.940Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Concurrent disjoint --add-ac additions on separate branches all survive a merge, or the delimiter-joined scalar semantics are documented at src/core/item/parse.ts, in pm update --help, and in the merge guidance; Every field whose CLI grammar exposes additive and subtractive mutation is either a union collection or is listed as a known-lossy scalar in one enumerable place the merge driver and the docs both read; A merge that discards acceptance criteria names acceptance_criteria and the number of discarded criteria in the receipt guidance rather than reporting a generic scalar conflict"
value: Acceptance criteria are the machine-readable definition of done; losing them on merge silently weakens every close-time check built on them.
impact: "Any two agents that add criteria to the same item on different branches lose all but one contribution, and the close validation that reads criteria cannot tell."
outcome: "Either acceptance criteria merge by element identity like every other list-shaped field, or the docstring and the CLI help state the scalar semantics and pm warns when a merge discards criteria."
why_now: The same probe that falsified merge-direction independence falsified this documented guarantee; the fix is small and the loss is unrecoverable.
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: git merge via pm merge drivers; pm 2026.8.2
repro_steps: "Create an item on a base commit, branch three ways, run pm update <id> --add-ac 'criterion from A|B|C' on each branch, commit, then merge all three branches into one clone."
resolution: "The three-way item merge parses acceptance criteria into canonical elements, composes concurrent additions and removals, preserves legacy scalar serialization, reports the field as a union, and is protected by a focused negative-control gate."
expected_result: Concurrent additive and subtractive acceptance-criteria mutations merge without silent loss and expose field-specific merge evidence.
actual_result: "Three-branch additions and both-side removals pass focused regression coverage without a scalar conflict decision; exact coverage, typecheck, static assurance, and defect-evidence gates pass."
component: core/item/parse
