comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T17:36:05.568Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence: TDD reproduced scalar loss, then the item merge driver began parsing acceptance_criteria through the canonical parser and applying the same add/remove-aware three-way union used by native collections while preserving the legacy serialized shape. Multi-branch A/B/C additions survive, either-side removals remain removed, union_fields names acceptance_criteria, and no scalar conflict decision is emitted. Focused linked tests passed 3/3; repo-wide coverage passed exactly 59387/59387 lines, 61714/61714 statements, 12840/12840 functions, and 46669/46669 branches; typecheck and the complete static/graph/history assurance pipeline passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T17:36:06.552Z","harness:codex","A delimiter-backed field with additive CLI grammar must be merged as parsed elements, not as its serialized scalar; storage compatibility does not justify lossy concurrency semantics."
